              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Tiu-U é‡£é­š is a domino card game that involves tiles, matching, scoring. The game originated in China and has become popular worldwide."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Country/Region of Origin: China\nTime Period: Early 1900s\nHistorical Development: The game evolved from traditional card games in the region\nCultural Significance: Popular social and family game"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Setup",
          "subtitle": "Table, deck, equipment, and deal",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Minimum Players: 2\nMaximum Players: 3\nOptimal Players: 3\nPartnerships: None"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Type: Chinese dominoes\nNumber of Sets: 2 (64 tiles total)\nJokers: Not used"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Two sets of Chinese dominoes (64 tiles)\nTable space for woodpile and layout"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Tiles in woodpile (four high). Four stacks (16 tiles) laid face up. Two players: three stacks each (12 tiles). Three players: two stacks each (8 tiles)."
